      "lineHeight": {
        "$description": "Line-height scale (unitless), named by percent: 150 is 1.5 (2026-11-17; it used to have word names: tight 120, normal 150, and none 100, snug 135 and relaxed 170, removed on 2026-11-18 because nothing used them). Headings and Display take theirs from one curve through H6 (130) and H1 (110): H5 122, H4 117, H3 114, H2 112, Display 108, 106, 105, 104, 103. Text uses 150. 120 is used only by today's styles, until they move to the new set.",
